{number: 28}
{title: While Shepherds Watched Their Flocks}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] While shepherds watched their [A] flocks by night,
All [D] seated [A7] on the [D] ground;
The angel of the [A] Lord came down,
And [D] glory [G] shone a-[D] round,
"Fear [A] not!" said he,
for [D] mighty dread had seized their [A] troubled mind.
"Glad [D] tidings of great [G] joy I bring
to [D] all of [A7] human-[D] kind."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
"To [D] you, in David's [A] town,
This day is [D] born of [A7] David's [D] line a Savior,
Who is Christ the [A] Lord,
and [D] this shall [G] be the [D] sign, and this shall be the sign:"
"The [A] heavenly babe you [D] there shall find
To human [A] view displayed,
All [D] meanly wrapped in [G] swathing bands,
And [D] in a [A7] manger [D] laid."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Thus [D] spake the seraph [A] and forthwith
ap-[D] peared a [A7] shining [D] throng
of angels praising [A] God on high,
who [D] thus ad-[G] dressed their [D] song:
"All [A] glory be to [D] God on high,
And to the [A] earth be peace;
Good [D] will henceforth from [G] heaven to earth
Be-[D] gin and [A7] never [D] cease!"
{end_of_verse}
